WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.034
This is the first time that

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.602
Santos admitted that he lied

00:00:02.602 --> 00:00:04.671
about key details in his resume.

00:00:04.971 --> 00:00:05.872
He said in an interview

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:06.740
with the New York Post

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:08.141
and a local radio station

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:09.542
that he did not actually work

00:00:09.542 --> 00:00:10.276
for Citigroup. Corp.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:11.511
or for Goldman Sachs,

00:00:11.511 --> 00:00:11.778
even though

00:00:11.778 --> 00:00:13.646
previously on the campaign trail,

00:00:13.646 --> 00:00:14.948
he said he did.

00:00:14.948 --> 00:00:16.116
Now, Santos is saying

00:00:16.116 --> 00:00:17.817
that he only worked for them

00:00:17.817 --> 00:00:19.119
through his company,

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:19.819
and so he called it

00:00:19.819 --> 00:00:21.588
a poor choice of words to suggest

00:00:21.588 --> 00:00:23.590
that he worked directly for those firms.

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:24.991
But Santos also admitted

00:00:24.991 --> 00:00:25.992
that he never graduated

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:27.694
from any college or university

00:00:27.694 --> 00:00:29.162
after previously claiming

00:00:29.162 --> 00:00:30.930
that he received degrees from both

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.966
NYU and Baruch College.

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.567
Now, he said he was embarrassed

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:35.335
and that essentially

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:36.036
he just chalked it up

00:00:36.036 --> 00:00:37.570
to embellishing his resume

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:38.638
and that everyone did it.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:39.706
So essentially,

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:40.874
he was trying to downplay

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.242
this entire controversy.

00:00:42.242 --> 00:00:43.076
And he said

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:43.643
while he is

00:00:43.643 --> 00:00:45.211
guilty of twisting the truth,

00:00:45.211 --> 00:00:46.713
he is not guilty of committing

00:00:46.713 --> 00:00:48.081
any crimes. Take a listen.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.485
I'm not a criminal, not here,

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:54.220
not abroad

00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:56.423
in any jurisdiction in the world.

00:00:56.423 --> 00:00:58.892
Have I ever committed any crimes

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.693
to get down to the Nitty-Gritty?

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.028
I'm not a fraud.

00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.897
I'm not a criminal

00:01:03.897 --> 00:01:05.832
who defrauded the entire country

00:01:05.832 --> 00:01:07.200
and made up this fictitious

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.169
character and ran for Congress.

00:01:09.169 --> 00:01:10.670
I've been around a long time.

00:01:10.670 --> 00:01:12.372
I mean, a lot of people know me.

00:01:12.372 --> 00:01:13.206
They know who I am.

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.808
They've been business dealings with me.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:15.742
And I'm not going to

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.843
make excuses for this.

00:01:16.843 --> 00:01:19.412
But my a lot of people overstate

00:01:19.412 --> 00:01:21.381
in their resumes or

00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:24.284
twist a little bit or in grandeur

00:01:24.350 --> 00:01:24.984
themselves.

00:01:24.984 --> 00:01:28.855
I'm not saying I'm not guilty of that.

00:01:28.855 --> 00:01:30.857
Now, Santos did not answer questions

00:01:30.857 --> 00:01:32.192
about his charity's

00:01:32.192 --> 00:01:32.559
claims

00:01:32.559 --> 00:01:33.093
that he made

00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:34.227
about his heritage

00:01:34.227 --> 00:01:34.861
and questions

00:01:34.861 --> 00:01:36.496
about his financial disclosures

00:01:36.496 --> 00:01:38.598
and whether he followed proper protocols.

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:40.233
And so there's still a lot there

00:01:40.233 --> 00:01:40.967
that we don't know

00:01:40.967 --> 00:01:42.168
that is unanswered for.

00:01:42.168 --> 00:01:42.735
I suspect

00:01:42.735 --> 00:01:43.770
this will not quell

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:44.537
the calls

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:46.639
for him to not serve in Congress.

00:01:46.639 --> 00:01:47.340
So far, however,

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:48.675
Palm GOP leaders are silent.

00:01:49.742 --> 00:01:50.343
Well,

00:01:50.343 --> 00:01:50.910
we'll have to wait

00:01:50.910 --> 00:01:52.412
and see if it stays that way

00:01:52.412 --> 00:01:53.313
after this interview.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.347
Did he say why

00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:55.515
he made those statements

00:01:55.515 --> 00:01:57.117
in the first place?

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:58.318
What was his reasoning,

00:01:58.318 --> 00:01:59.352
for example, saying

00:01:59.352 --> 00:02:00.420
that he graduated from

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.555
these had degrees from these colleges

00:02:02.555 --> 00:02:04.824
and yet he never had a college degree?

00:02:05.091 --> 00:02:05.291
Yeah,

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:06.659
he didn't really give the reasoning.

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:08.228
Other than trying to suggest that it's

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:10.296
a common trait to lie on your resume

00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:12.365
or to embellish embellish a little bit.

00:02:12.365 --> 00:02:14.100
But this is a big deal.

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:15.268
He is about to serve

00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.503
as a member of Congress.

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:18.771
He misrepresented who he was.

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.039
In normal circumstances,

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:21.141
if someone lied on their resume,

00:02:21.141 --> 00:02:22.775
they probably would be fired.

00:02:22.775 --> 00:02:23.610
But in this case, it's

00:02:23.610 --> 00:02:24.911
up to the voters to decide.

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.379
And if he chooses to stick around,

00:02:26.379 --> 00:02:27.347
there's not much

00:02:27.347 --> 00:02:28.214
anyone can do

00:02:28.214 --> 00:02:30.283
unless Congress decides not to seat him.

00:02:30.283 --> 00:02:31.217
But that is decision

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:33.486
up to GOP leader Kevin McCarthy.

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:34.621
And as a right now,

00:02:34.621 --> 00:02:35.588
like I said, he's silent

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:37.023
and he probably needs every speaker vote

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:37.991
he can get next week.

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.292
Yeah, he does

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.760
wonder if that's a factor in all of this.

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.729
Melanie, as an owner, thank you so much.

00:02:42.729 --> 00:02:43.463
Perspective now

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:44.998
from CNN political commentator Scott

00:02:44.998 --> 00:02:46.499
Jennings, former special assistant

00:02:46.499 --> 00:02:48.201
to President George W Bush.

00:02:48.201 --> 00:02:49.569
Also CNN political

00:02:49.569 --> 00:02:51.171
analyst and Axios managing

00:02:51.171 --> 00:02:52.472
editor Margaret Talev.

00:02:52.472 --> 00:02:52.672
All right,

00:02:52.672 --> 00:02:54.240
Margaret, starting with you here.

00:02:54.240 --> 00:02:56.509
So Congressman elect Santos

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.810
has admitted to essentially

00:02:57.810 --> 00:03:00.713
fabricating his entire resume

00:03:00.780 --> 00:03:02.215
top to bottom.

00:03:02.215 --> 00:03:05.685
He downplayed it as resumé embellishment,

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.220
something we all do all

00:03:07.220 --> 00:03:08.988
we all embellish our resumes.

00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:10.557
Is that all this is

00:03:12.959 --> 00:03:13.293
it?

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:15.395
You literally can't believe anything

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:15.995
he says.

00:03:15.995 --> 00:03:17.964
It's not just not that

00:03:17.964 --> 00:03:18.631
any of this is okay.

00:03:18.631 --> 00:03:20.233
It's not just his job.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:20.767
History is not

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:23.803
just his educational history.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.605
Even down to his claim

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:28.708
that that one of his companies

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:30.076
had lost four employees

00:03:30.076 --> 00:03:32.111
in the Pulse nightclub shooting

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.079
six years ago.

00:03:33.079 --> 00:03:35.315
Turns out that's not actually true.

00:03:35.782 --> 00:03:36.516
There are people who

00:03:36.516 --> 00:03:37.984
maybe we're going to go to work for,

00:03:37.984 --> 00:03:39.219
like your questions

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.521
about his background in Brazil.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:43.089
But there are a myriad of questions.

00:03:43.089 --> 00:03:44.591
But the bottom line is,

00:03:44.591 --> 00:03:45.391
here's the question.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.594
What could block him from being seated?

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:48.928
Probably nothing.

00:03:48.928 --> 00:03:50.597
There are age requirements

00:03:50.597 --> 00:03:52.799
and citizenship requirements

00:03:52.799 --> 00:03:56.502
to be seated in Congress.

00:03:56.502 --> 00:03:58.504
As far as we know, he's still 34

00:03:58.504 --> 00:04:01.140
and he's old enough to serve in that job.

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:02.909
So and then and of course, remember,

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:05.178
Kevin McCarthy does need his vote

00:04:05.178 --> 00:04:05.645
coming forth

00:04:05.645 --> 00:04:06.813
and needs every vote

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:07.780
in the Republican caucus

00:04:07.780 --> 00:04:10.016
to send him speakership just about.

00:04:10.049 --> 00:04:12.752
So this really may be an instance

00:04:12.752 --> 00:04:13.753
where the question is, is

00:04:13.753 --> 00:04:15.054
he going to face

00:04:15.054 --> 00:04:16.856
ethics investigations in Congress?

00:04:16.856 --> 00:04:17.490
And again,

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:19.492
the answer to that question right now

00:04:19.492 --> 00:04:21.060
may well be no.

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:22.662
The attorney general in New York

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:23.997
has said that her office is

00:04:23.997 --> 00:04:24.931
going to look into

00:04:25.932 --> 00:04:27.500
investigating his background.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:30.503
But again, this really may be an issue

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:31.838
for voters. Two years from now.

00:04:31.838 --> 00:04:33.673
It's an astonishing story.

00:04:33.673 --> 00:04:35.041
And the congressional district

00:04:35.041 --> 00:04:36.576
is one of the wealthiest in the country.

00:04:36.576 --> 00:04:37.277
He's a very,

00:04:37.277 --> 00:04:39.412
very one who engaged voters

00:04:39.445 --> 00:04:40.880
where they should be.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:41.314
Right.

00:04:41.314 --> 00:04:42.382
I mean, they were voting for

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:43.750
someone based on a resume

00:04:43.750 --> 00:04:45.785
that was that was false. Right.

00:04:46.352 --> 00:04:49.022
Santos Scott has vowed to be sworn

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.823
in to Congress and serve his term.

00:04:50.823 --> 00:04:53.393
Now, as Margaret laid out.

00:04:53.393 --> 00:04:54.327
There's really not a whole lot

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:55.261
you can do to prevent

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:56.729
that from happening.

00:04:56.729 --> 00:04:58.364
But do you think he should bow out

00:04:58.364 --> 00:04:59.299
or do you think that

00:04:59.299 --> 00:05:00.466
he should still move forward

00:05:00.466 --> 00:05:03.336
as he has said he will do?

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:04.437
You know, honestly,

00:05:04.437 --> 00:05:06.773
if he hadn't a shred of self integrity,

00:05:06.973 --> 00:05:07.740
you know,

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.041
he would

00:05:08.041 --> 00:05:08.708
he would bow out

00:05:08.708 --> 00:05:11.177
because he made up a whole story,

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:12.245
sold it to the voters,

00:05:12.245 --> 00:05:13.446
and he got elected.

00:05:13.446 --> 00:05:14.881
And so if he really meant

00:05:14.881 --> 00:05:16.516
what he said in his interviews today,

00:05:16.516 --> 00:05:17.717
he would resign

00:05:17.717 --> 00:05:19.986
and then run on his actual resume.

00:05:20.553 --> 00:05:21.487
And see what the voters

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:22.422
had to say at that point.

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.357
I mean, that would be sort of the honest

00:05:24.357 --> 00:05:25.558
and honorable way to handle it.

00:05:25.558 --> 00:05:26.793
He's obviously not going to do that.

00:05:26.793 --> 00:05:27.193
I mean,

00:05:27.193 --> 00:05:28.061
you don't want to play golf

00:05:28.061 --> 00:05:29.195
or cards with this guy.

00:05:29.195 --> 00:05:29.896
I do say

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:32.265
I do think you want to see this guy

00:05:32.265 --> 00:05:33.533
put before the Ethics Committee.

00:05:33.533 --> 00:05:34.901
It strikes me that he may have financial

00:05:34.901 --> 00:05:36.135
disclosure issues

00:05:37.236 --> 00:05:38.371
and it

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:39.872
also has the smell

00:05:39.872 --> 00:05:41.641
the whiff of other shoes

00:05:41.641 --> 00:05:42.575
that are about to drop.

00:05:42.575 --> 00:05:43.476
I don't know anything.

00:05:43.476 --> 00:05:44.877
And we've got reporters working on it.

00:05:44.877 --> 00:05:46.646
But you just get the feeling,

00:05:46.646 --> 00:05:48.781
even after all we learned today,

00:05:48.781 --> 00:05:50.883
there could be more so.

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:51.718
Look, it's

00:05:51.718 --> 00:05:52.985
obviously not an honorable person.

00:05:52.985 --> 00:05:54.487
I doubt he resigns.

00:05:54.487 --> 00:05:56.823
And if the voters get a chance to

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:57.790
deal with it in two years,

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.058
I'm sure they will.

00:05:59.058 --> 00:05:59.592
Yeah.

00:05:59.592 --> 00:06:00.993
A reporter is looking at everything.

00:06:00.993 --> 00:06:03.129
The financial disclosure is so much more

00:06:03.129 --> 00:06:05.898
because he has not addressed other issues

00:06:05.898 --> 00:06:07.066
that have come up as Melanie

00:06:07.066 --> 00:06:08.101
shot him in the charities

00:06:08.101 --> 00:06:09.635
that were listed on his resume.

00:06:09.635 --> 00:06:11.571
So House Republican Leader Kevin McCarthy

00:06:11.571 --> 00:06:14.240
so far hasn't addressed this controversy

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:15.742
as we've laid out.

00:06:15.742 --> 00:06:17.343
More could come out

00:06:17.343 --> 00:06:19.245
now, but Santos has admitted this.

00:06:19.245 --> 00:06:21.080
So Mark. Margaret, what do you think?

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:22.882
I mean, can he continue to ignore this?

00:06:24.817 --> 00:06:25.284
I mean,

00:06:26.052 --> 00:06:26.519
is there really

00:06:26.519 --> 00:06:28.388
going to be ask about this

00:06:28.388 --> 00:06:30.656
and Santos, every place

00:06:30.656 --> 00:06:32.658
he goes, every corner in town.

00:06:32.658 --> 00:06:33.359
What committees

00:06:33.359 --> 00:06:35.962
to the person you serve on

00:06:35.962 --> 00:06:37.397
if you're a constituent

00:06:37.397 --> 00:06:38.931
and you are

00:06:38.931 --> 00:06:40.433
trying to engage with them, like

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:42.468
how much money

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:44.337
can you put in his response?

00:06:44.337 --> 00:06:45.271
I think this is a real

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:47.106
credibility problem.

00:06:47.106 --> 00:06:49.342
But in terms of what's going to happen,

00:06:49.342 --> 00:06:50.376
it certainly seems like

00:06:50.376 --> 00:06:51.611
he is going to be seated

00:06:51.611 --> 00:06:53.379
in Congress again.

00:06:53.379 --> 00:06:55.081
All right, Margaret, Scott,

00:06:55.081 --> 00:06:55.748
great to see you.

00:06:55.748 --> 00:06:56.949
Thanks for coming on tonight.

